[# email/mobile-only: sections that only show on phones (below 480px wide).

   Uses the hide-desktop class from layouts/base.mjml. The content is hidden by default and shown by a media query,
   so clients that ignore media queries never show it. That includes Outlook desktop, which is correct for a
   mobile-only block.

   Compatibility
   - Outlook desktop: never shown (it ignores media queries), by design.
   - Gmail apps: shown on phones. Gmail on non-Google accounts drops media queries, so it stays hidden there.
   - Dark mode: nothing extra, the sections inside carry their own colors. #]
<mj-wrapper css-class="hide-desktop" padding="0">
  [[ data.content ]]
</mj-wrapper>
